From ea5a34084ec578383252bab4b6e887c0428afc0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:58:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Japanese support and table-aware Suggest mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Japanese UI (window, settings, overlay messages, chat notices) with a
  language setting (Auto / English / Japanese); kanji tile names in Japanese.
- Recognize Japanese game strings: seat winds (東南西北), riichi badge,
  and call buttons (ロン/ツモ/リーチ/ポン/チー/カン/九種九牌/パス...).
  Call-button matching moved to EmjStrings with a guarded pass fallback.
- Suggest mode now runs the same TurnPolicy as auto-play (visible tiles,
  dora, fold vs riichi, furiten dodge, riichi call), shows accepted tiles,
  opponents in riichi, ron availability and tsumogiri while in riichi.
- One shared LiveBoard for window and overlay; policy results cached.
- Settings: reset auto-play delays. Linux builds skip the PowerShell
  icon-bundling step.
- TurnDecision exposes a TurnReason kind; tests for string matching and
  tile names; README.ja.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JdRV9wQ5A5yrwpkc3PSQqt
